1. Definitions

"Core Group" means the Constellation Overwatch maintainers or any legal entity
they designate to administer commercial licensing.

"Commercial Use" means private-sector use of the Software, in whole or in part,
by or for a for-profit entity, in connection with revenue-generating activity,
in a product or service offered to third parties, as part of paid consulting or
managed services, or in production operations for a business purpose.

"Government and Military Use" means use of the Software by a government,
military, public-sector, public safety, emergency response, educational, or
public research organization for that organization's own mission, operations,
evaluation, training, research, or internal deployment.

"Community Use" means personal, hobby, research, educational, evaluation,
Government and Military Use, or other noncommercial use that is not Commercial
Use.

"Modified Version" means any copy of the Software that has been changed,
adapted, translated, extended, linked into, combined with, or otherwise used to
create a derivative work requiring permission under copyright law.

"Corresponding Source" means the complete preferred form of the Software and any
Modified Version for making modifications, including build scripts, interface
definitions, configuration files, installation instructions, and other materials
reasonably necessary to build, run, test, and modify the work.

2. Community Use Grant

Subject to this license, the Core Group grants you a worldwide, royalty-free,
