3. Copyleft and Share-Back Requirements

If you distribute, publish, provide access to, or make available a Modified
Version, including by operating it as a network service for users outside your
personal household or hobby environment, you must:

a. license the Modified Version under this same license;

b. make the complete Corresponding Source for the Modified Version publicly
available at no charge from a durable, readily accessible location;

c. include a clear notice describing the changes you made and the date of those
changes;

d. preserve all copyright, license, attribution, and required notices; and

e. notify the Core Group of the public source location by pull request, issue,
or email to info@yeetum.com.

These requirements apply whether the Modified Version is distributed as source
code, object code, a container image, an appliance, a hosted service, or any
other form.

4. Commercial Use

Government and Military Use is permitted under this community license when the
Software is used directly by a government, military, public-sector, public
safety, emergency response, educational, or public research organization for its
own mission or operations.

Commercial Use is not permitted under this community license. Before any
Commercial Use, you must obtain a separate paid commercial license or written
commercial-use agreement from the Core Group.

Private-sector vendors, contractors, subcontractors, systems integrators,
consultants, managed-service providers, cloud providers, and other for-profit
entities do not receive free Government and Military Use rights merely because
their customer, sponsor, funder, or end user is a government, military, or
public-sector organization.

Commercial licenses may include support, private modification rights, hosted
deployment rights, revenue sharing, sponsorship, contribution obligations, or
other payback terms agreed in writing with the Core Group.

